    "body": "<html>\n<body>\n<!--StartFragment--><p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Negative results: six sweeps on the RO1 model, all no match</strong></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Same anchors and pools as <code dir=\"ltr\">reading-order-pool.json</code> (dutch at 1, fog at 5, parrot at 12). Every run passed a selftest first: the canonical <code dir=\"ltr\">abandon…about</code> vector, agreement with bip_utils, and a planted witness recovered through the real enumeration.</p>\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\nRO1 on 7 paths (/0/0–/0/4, 1'/0/0, 2'/0/0): 167,688,000 arrangements, 10,484,919 checksum-valid, all 7 paths\nRO1 + free video slot from atom, link, basic, token, dash: 1,741,140,000 arrangements, 108,817,960 valid, default path\nRO1 + free video slot from build, ready: 696,456,000 arrangements, 43,524,282 valid, default path\nRO1 + free video slot from donor, stay, until, win: 1,392,912,000 arrangements, 87,064,878 valid, default path\nRO1 + free post-side floater \"hard\": 125,766,000 arrangements, 7,863,418 valid, default path\nRO1 + free post-side floater \"minimum\": 348,228,000 arrangements, 21,763,738 valid, default path\n\n</div>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What this rules out:</strong> the RO1 space on the alternative derivation paths (lead 3), plus the extra-word variants above at <code dir=\"ltr\">m/44'/60'/0'/0/0</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>What it does not rule out:</strong> anything outside RO1's reading-order model, checksum-invalid phrases (only valid candidates were derived), and the other paths for the extra-word sweeps.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Scripts:</strong> <code dir=\"ltr\">sweep_paths.py</code>, <code dir=\"ltr\">sweep_coins.py</code> and <code dir=\"ltr\">sweep_postword.py</code> import the enumeration from <code dir=\"ltr\">sweep_reading_order.py</code> unchanged. Each has <code dir=\"ltr\">--selftest</code> and <code dir=\"ltr\">--run --resume</code>. Speed is about 1,000 derivations/s per core, so the paths sweep took about 13 minutes on 22 workers.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Next:</strong> the connecting-words lead (about 1.36e10 derivations) needs a GPU PBKDF2 implementation. If anyone has one, I'd welcome it.</p><!--EndFragment-->\n</body>\n</html>\n\n[sweep_postword.py](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32678410/sweep_postword.py)\n[sweep_coins.py](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32678411/sweep_coins.py)\n[sweep_paths.py](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32678409/sweep_paths.py)",
